00:20:51,917 --> 00:20:54,378
-I mean, the heels--
-Are there expectations?

486
00:20:54,670 --> 00:20:57,047
I think people probably have expectations.

487
00:20:57,130 --> 00:20:59,758
And it sounds like you're more of a, like,

488
00:20:59,841 --> 00:21:03,095
"Listen, whatever I can do to you,
you can do to me" type of person?

489
00:21:03,178 --> 00:21:06,348
Mmm... I'd say I'm... I'm very dominant
in most situations.

490
00:21:06,431 --> 00:21:07,557
-Oh.
-Yeah.

491
00:21:07,641 --> 00:21:10,435
-Wow.
-I'm very driven by being told, like,

492
00:21:10,519 --> 00:21:12,104
"No, you can't do this"--

493
00:21:12,187 --> 00:21:14,064
I don't think
we should have a second date.

494
00:21:14,147 --> 00:21:15,899
Well, challenge accepted.

495
00:21:15,983 --> 00:21:16,817
Oh, okay.

496
00:21:18,068 --> 00:21:20,404
-I really enjoyed my first blind date.
-[Cory] Yeah?

497
00:21:20,612 --> 00:21:21,655
Were you nervous at all?

498
00:21:22,239 --> 00:21:23,115
Mmm...

499
00:21:23,532 --> 00:21:24,366
no.

500
00:21:24,574 --> 00:21:27,452
It is kind of exciting, right,
to meet a complete stranger?

501
00:21:27,536 --> 00:21:28,537
-Totally.
-Yeah.

502
00:21:28,620 --> 00:21:30,122
Yeah, I feel like a lot of people...

503
00:21:31,039 --> 00:21:32,791
do that for different reasons online.

504
00:21:32,874 --> 00:21:34,876
[both laughing]

505
00:21:35,043 --> 00:21:37,421
True. Ours are quite innocent
by comparison.

506
00:21:37,504 --> 00:21:41,049
I'm... I'm really glad that my first blind
date wasn't blindfolded ass-up.

507
00:21:41,300 --> 00:21:42,634
'Cause that would be awkward.

508
00:21:42,884 --> 00:21:44,970
-Do you want to share a Lyft home?
-Yeah.

509
00:21:45,053 --> 00:21:46,930
Well, um...

510
00:21:47,597 --> 00:21:49,891
Yeah, maybe we should get out of here.

511
00:21:50,600 --> 00:21:52,644
Let's go. After you.

512
00:21:52,936 --> 00:21:54,187
Oh, shit. Okay.

513
00:22:01,278 --> 00:22:04,197
Do you mind making the air, like,
 a little lower, please?

514
00:22:16,877 --> 00:22:17,794
Well, um...

515
00:22:19,129 --> 00:22:21,423
I feel like I should get your number.

516
00:22:21,715 --> 00:22:22,549
Okay.

517
00:22:22,632 --> 00:22:23,759
-Right?
-Yeah.

518
00:22:23,842 --> 00:22:25,010
'Cause, like...

519
00:22:25,552 --> 00:22:27,012
Gotta get my phone out.

520
00:22:27,095 --> 00:22:27,929
Here.

521
00:22:29,264 --> 00:22:31,224
We never even did last names, right?

522
00:22:32,142 --> 00:22:36,938
No, because I know exactly what's gonna
happen if I give you my last name.

523
00:22:37,022 --> 00:22:38,190
[Cory chuckles]

524
00:22:38,857 --> 00:22:43,153
'Cause I was doing most of the talking,
I felt that you weren't that into me.

525
00:22:43,236 --> 00:22:45,489
So, I want to know
if you're interested in, like...

526
00:22:46,073 --> 00:22:48,325
meeting, like, for another date?

527
00:22:51,244 --> 00:22:52,120
Um...

528
00:22:53,163 --> 00:22:54,706
I don't know about another date,

529
00:22:54,790 --> 00:22:56,875
-but I would definitely be interested in--
-Friendship?

530
00:22:57,376 --> 00:22:59,002
-Yeah.
-No, that's great.

531
00:22:59,086 --> 00:22:59,920
[Lex] Let's do it.

532
00:23:00,087 --> 00:23:03,006
-Pleasure to meet you, Peter.
-Likewise. Let's do this again soon.

533
00:23:03,090 --> 00:23:05,133
-Yeah. For sure. Good night.
-You too.

534
00:23:10,138 --> 00:23:11,598
[Jonathan] I can't open this door.

535
00:23:12,224 --> 00:23:14,393
This almost looks like an ashtray,
the way it's set up.

536
00:23:14,810 --> 00:23:16,520
But it's actually the handle of the door.

537
00:23:18,230 --> 00:23:20,148
Good night. Thanks.

538
00:23:22,317 --> 00:23:24,653
-So, this is my stop.
-All right, Brad.

539
00:23:26,029 --> 00:23:28,073
-[Lex] Hope to see you soon?
-Absolutely.

540
00:23:28,156 --> 00:23:29,241
Okay. Let's make it happen.

541
00:23:29,533 --> 00:23:31,201
You'll text or call?

542
00:23:31,284 --> 00:23:32,494
-I will.
-All right.

543
00:23:33,036 --> 00:23:34,663
-[Cory] I had a really good time.
-Me too.

544
00:23:35,122 --> 00:23:37,624
-Goodnight.
-Okay. Have a good night.

545
00:23:39,334 --> 00:23:40,168
[Cory] Bye.

546
00:23:42,212 --> 00:23:44,506
[sighs]

547
00:23:45,924 --> 00:23:46,925
[sighs wearily]

548
00:23:51,179 --> 00:23:53,181
["Reunion" playing]

549
00:24:07,779 --> 00:24:10,198
♪ You came out of nowhere ♪

550
00:24:11,533 --> 00:24:14,453
♪ Stealing my heart and brain ♪

551
00:24:15,537 --> 00:24:18,248
♪ Flaming my every cell ♪

552
00:24:19,040 --> 00:24:19,875
[man] Hi.

553
00:24:20,625 --> 00:24:21,710
Hey.

554
00:24:21,918 --> 00:24:24,504
-How're you doing?
-How are you, Daddy Longlegs?

555
00:24:24,588 --> 00:24:26,840
-[Cory] Good to see you.
-Good to see you too.

556
00:24:27,007 --> 00:24:28,800
-Ooh, it's warm today.
-I know.

557
00:24:28,884 --> 00:24:30,385
Do you have high heels on your shirt?

558
00:24:31,136 --> 00:24:34,306
I do. I mean, I figure if I'm gonna go
on a date with a baby giraffe,

559
00:24:34,389 --> 00:24:36,308
-I should wear my heels.
-[Cory laughs]

560
00:24:36,558 --> 00:24:37,476
No, you look good.

561
00:24:37,559 --> 00:24:39,769
-I'm glad you came.
-Well, that's really good to hear.

562
00:24:39,853 --> 00:24:42,689
-Um, if you want to go in, I have tickets.
-Let's do it.

563
00:24:44,566 --> 00:24:45,775
[Lex] So...

564
00:24:46,568 --> 00:24:47,569
did you stalk me?

565
00:24:48,111 --> 00:24:49,237
I didn't yet.

566
00:24:49,321 --> 00:24:50,822
-You didn't? Really?
-I didn't.

567
00:24:50,906 --> 00:24:52,908
[Cory] Um, I don't know your last name.

568
00:24:53,867 --> 00:24:54,743
[Lex] Oh.

